# Fire Lord Sozin: "Whenever Fire Lord Sozin deals combat damage to a player, you may pay {X}. When you do, put any number of
# target creature cards with total mana value X or less from that player's graveyard onto the battlefield under your control."
#
# Bot2 casts Ornithopter, two Llanowar Elves and Guerrilla Gorilla on T2; Bot1's The Rise of Sozin (cast on T3 off two Swamps, Dark
# Ritual and Black Lotus) destroys them all with chapter I, Bot1's own Ornithopter too. Chapter III on T7 returns it as Fire Lord
# Sozin, which attacks on T9: firebending 3 adds {R}{R}{R}, and in the combat damage step Bot1 pays X = 1 out of it (CR 107.3f:
# X chosen as it is paid). The reflexive ability (CR 603.12) is put on the stack with X = 1 and its targets are chosen then
# (CR 603.3d, 601.2c): Guerrilla Gorilla (mana value 2) is worth more than X by itself and is no candidate; the two Elves together
# (total 2) are refused; Bot1's own Ornithopter is in the wrong graveyard. Ornithopter (0) and one Elves (1) make 1, and enter under
# Bot1's control; the {R}{R} left over is lost as combat ends.

